cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  trajectory-eval-harness: an evaluation framework for LLM-agent
  reliability that scores intermediate reasoning steps
message: If you reference this work, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Xinyang
    family-names: Qiao
abstract: >-
  An evaluation framework for LLM-agent reliability that scores intermediate
  reasoning steps rather than final outputs. Six trajectory-level scorers run
  over a frozen JSONL schema: pass^k stability, gate integrity (whether an
  escalation fires AND whether it fires for the stated reason), agreement
  against a human reference, internal ledger consistency, tool-call
  correctness, and an evidence-coverage sentinel. Demonstrated on a resume-job
  description screening agent with a human-in-the-loop gate, across two model
  providers, with constructed fault cases and three rounds of prompt-injection
  defense. The central result is a model-selection reversal - the candidate
  model scored better on every outcome metric while trajectory metrics showed
  it never judged requirements fully met, so it escalated every case.
keywords:
  - llm evaluation
  - agent evaluation
  - trajectory analysis
  - human-in-the-loop
  - prompt injection
  - langgraph
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/xy9iao/trajectory-eval-harness
url: https://github.com/xy9iao/trajectory-eval-harness/blob/main/docs/final-report.md
date-released: '2026-08-04'
